      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma (1. your folder)</b> - Point it at a folder and pick the pictures. Press Run once and it sends every picture through the workflow, one after the other. Its <b>filename</b> output carries each picture's name to the save node, and <b>index</b> says which picture it is (1, 2, 3 ...).</li><li><b>Number Pixaroma (2. new size in percent)</b> - The new size in percent: 50 = half the size, 200 = twice the size.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The helpers</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Purple. They run by themselves and do the small jobs: count, pick, join or pass things along.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Math Expression (new width = a x b / 100)</b> - Works out the new width for EACH picture: <code>round(a * b / 100)</code> = the picture's width x the percent / 100, rounded to whole pixels. <b>a</b> is wired from the folder node's width, <b>b</b> from the percent.</li><li><b>Math Expression (new height = a x b / 100)</b> - The same for the height: <code>round(a * b / 100)</code> with the picture's height.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The work</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Green. They run by themselves.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Upscale Image (resizes to the new width and height)</b> - Resizes each picture to the width and height the Math nodes worked out, with lanczos, the sharpest method.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Save Image Pixaroma (3. where and how to save)</b> - Saves the resized pictures as JPG into <code>ComfyUI/output/Scaled</code>; the name gets the new size, like <code>01_Mug_512x512.jpg</code>.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Show Text Pixaroma (the new widths)</b> - Shows the new widths it worked out, one per picture, so you can check the maths.</li><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma (1. your folder)</b> - Point it at a folder and pick the pictures. Press Run once and it sends every picture through the workflow, one after the other. Its <b>filename</b> output carries each picture's name to the save node, and <b>index</b> says which picture it is (1, 2, 3 ...).</li><li><b>Number Pixaroma (2. new size in percent)</b> - The new size in percent: 50 = half the size, 200 = twice the size.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The helpers</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Purple. They run by themselves and do the small jobs: count, pick, join or pass things along.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Math Expression (new width = a x b / 100)</b> - Works out the new width for EACH picture: <code>round(a * b / 100)</code> = the picture's width x the percent / 100, rounded to whole pixels. <b>a</b> is wired from the folder node's width, <b>b</b> from the percent.</li><li><b>Math Expression (new height = a x b / 100)</b> - The same for the height: <code>round(a * b / 100)</code> with the picture's height.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\">